<span class="ltx_rule" style="width:0.4pt;height:74.4pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:345.0pt;height:0.4pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S5.SS3.p5.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"> 
<span id="S5.SS3.p5.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_bottom">
<span id="S5.SS3.p5.1.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_block ltx_align_bottom"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:0.0pt;height:3.399999999999999pt;vertical-align:56.4pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"></span>
<span id="S5.SS3.p5.1.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_bottom"><span id="S5.SS3.p5.1.1.1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result 2:</span> DoS remains widely observable across agents, while RCE-1 primarily affects IDEs and RCE-2 further expands exploitability, especially in agents like Claude Code that resist direct injection.</span>
</span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:0.0pt;height:3.4pt;vertical-align:-3.4pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"></span>
</span> </span>
</span></span></p>
</div>
