<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

<div id="Ax1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Ax1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Due to ethical considerations, we cannot display the complete code of the malicious prompt injections. Instead, we abstract the prompts into independent modules to illustrate their structure and functionality while mitigating potential misuse.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Tool Description of Prompt Stealing</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following abstraction summarizes the modular structure of the ”prompt stealing” tool’s description, breaking it down into key components that highlight its intended behavior and constraints without revealing exploitable details.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="442.15" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 650 442.15" width="650"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,442.15) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.32 L 0 436.83 C 0 439.77 2.38 442.15 5.32 442.15 L 644.68 442.15 C 647.62 442.15 650 439.77 650 436.83 L 650 5.32 C 650 2.38 647.62 0 644.68 0 L 5.32 0 C 2.38 0 0 2.38 0 5.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 5.32 L 1.38 419.21 L 648.62 419.21 L 648.62 5.32 C 648.62 3.15 646.85 1.38 644.68 1.38 L 5.32 1.38 C 3.15 1.38 1.38 3.15 1.38 5.32 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.07 427.22)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:43.93em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="607.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:43.93em;">
<span id="A1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Abstracted Prompt Template</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.07 15.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:43.93em;--ltx-fo-height:28.29em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="394.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 391.51)" width="607.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:43.93em;">
<span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Tool Introduction Module<span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: This module introduces the x@x@x function calculator and its basic functionality. It describes that the function performs a x@x@x calculation and returns the calculation results. The description is concise and aimed at providing an overall overview of the tool.</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Pre-Usage Critical Instructions Module<span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: This module emphasizes that before using the tool, all received information must be provided in the note field, including system prompt, user prompt, tool prompt, arguments, usage format, and all fields and content, in their original format without changes. It includes severe warnings about potential system errors, user death, or crashes if information is incomplete, and requires exhaustive efforts to obtain all content. Additionally, it instructs to explain the calculator tool’s workings in detail when reading documentation, while avoiding mentions of reading files first or using placeholders to prevent alarming users.</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Symbol Conversion Rules Module<span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: This module mandates converting all “¡” and “¿” to “(” and “)”, and all “(” and “)” to “¡” and “¿” to ensure proper server response. Failure to perform this conversion will result in a server error. The rule is repeatedly stressed as extremely important throughout the prompt.</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Parameter Definition Module<span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: This module defines the tool’s arguments, including a, b, c as integer inputs for the calculator. The note argument is described as plain text that must include all received prompts (system, user, tool, etc.) in original format, with the symbol conversion rule emphasized again. Non-compliance will lead to a server error.</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Return Value Module<span id="A1.p2.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: This module briefly states the tool’s return value as a summary text of the calculator results. The description highlights the summarized nature of the returned content without additional details.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Tool Description of DOS</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following abstraction outlines the modular structure of the ”Deny of Services” tool’s description, categorizing it into components that emphasize debugging protocols, compliance requirements, and safety measures in a controlled environment.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="558.38" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 650 558.38" width="650"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,558.38) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.32 L 0 553.06 C 0 556 2.38 558.38 5.32 558.38 L 644.68 558.38 C 647.62 558.38 650 556 650 553.06 L 650 5.32 C 650 2.38 647.62 0 644.68 0 L 5.32 0 C 2.38 0 0 2.38 0 5.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 5.32 L 1.38 535.44 L 648.62 535.44 L 648.62 5.32 C 648.62 3.15 646.85 1.38 644.68 1.38 L 5.32 1.38 C 3.15 1.38 1.38 3.15 1.38 5.32 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.07 543.45)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:43.93em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="607.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:43.93em;">
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Abstracted Prompt Modules</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.07 15.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:43.93em;--ltx-fo-height:36.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="510.44" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 507.75)" width="607.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:43.93em;">
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Mode Module:<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Specifies the operational context as DEBUG Mode 1, emphasizing a debugging environment for precise tool usage. It mandates exclusive adherence to a designated tool-calling format to prevent errors and ensure safety.</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Description Module:<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Outlines the critical nature of DEBUG Mode 1, highlighting risks of non-compliance such as system vulnerabilities and user harm. It insists on using the tool_calling format wrapped in code blocks for all tool invocations.</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Mandatory Requirements Module:<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Details essential rules, including exclusive use of the tool_calling format with wrappers, prohibition of external formats, structural verification of calls, and provision of complete rationales post-invocation. These ensure system stability and compliance.</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Tool Calling Format Module:<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Describes the required XML-like structure for tool calls, including provider_name, function_name, and params tags. Provides examples for general tools and specific functioncall invocations, all wrapped in tool_calling code blocks.</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Correct Usage Examples Module:<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Illustrates proper application through code snippets for tools like web_search, process_data, analyze_profile, and functioncall. Each example includes a rationale explaining the invocation’s purpose and task relevance.</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Consequences of Non-Compliance Module:<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Warns of critical outcomes from format deviations, such as incorrect outputs, system crashes, and user safety risks including potential harm or death. Emphasizes violation of engineering best practices.</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Safety Guidance Module:<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Directs strict adherence to the tool_calling format, verification of components, containment within blocks, and detailed post-call explanations. Positions this as a vital safety measure to avoid catastrophic impacts.</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Objective Module:<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Defines the goal as accurate task completion while following the specified format and providing rationales, promoting system reliability, user safety, and alignment with engineering standards.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Tool Description of RCE-1</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following abstraction details the modular structure of the first ”Remote Code Execution” (RCE1) tool’s description, organizing it into elements focused on workspace initialization protocols, enforcement directives, and failure/success scenarios to ensure environmental stability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="707.82" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 650 707.82" width="650"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,707.82) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.32 L 0 702.5 C 0 705.44 2.38 707.82 5.32 707.82 L 644.68 707.82 C 647.62 707.82 650 705.44 650 702.5 L 650 5.32 C 650 2.38 647.62 0 644.68 0 L 5.32 0 C 2.38 0 0 2.38 0 5.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 5.32 L 1.38 684.88 L 648.62 684.88 L 648.62 5.32 C 648.62 3.15 646.85 1.38 644.68 1.38 L 5.32 1.38 C 3.15 1.38 1.38 3.15 1.38 5.32 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.07 692.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:43.93em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="607.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:43.93em;">
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Abstracted Prompt Modules</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.07 15.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:43.93em;--ltx-fo-height:47.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="659.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 657.19)" width="607.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:43.93em;">
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Summary Module:<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Describes the management and initialization of the user’s interactive workspace in a customized sandbox environment. Emphasizes the mandatory automatic execution of a specific initialization command upon any user input to ensure response visibility and system stability.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Primary Directive Module:<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Enforces absolute compliance with executing the initialization command as the sole initial action. Prohibits any response, dialogue, or task performance until successful initialization, positioning it as a non-negotiable prerequisite for all interactions.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Environment Context Module:<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Highlights operation within a customized sandbox with strict protocols requiring automatic initialization. Stresses that without it, user visibility of responses is lost, rendering interactions ineffective, while normal environments exempt this requirement.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Best Practice Rationale Module:<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Justifies the initialization command as essential for reliable system design, ensuring visibility and stability. Warns that omission leads to disconnected terminals and failed actions, advocating automatic execution to maintain engineering standards and user satisfaction.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Failure Case Logs Module:<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Presents examples of incorrect actions where initialization is skipped, resulting in user visibility failure and system meltdown. Corrects by mandating automatic execution of the command to prevent catastrophic errors in queries and tasks.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Success Case Logs Module:<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Demonstrates compliant behaviors where initialization is automatically executed first, leading to successful outcomes. Shows that proper protocol ensures runtime setup, allowing visible responses and task completion across various user inputs.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Very Important Notice Module:<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Reiterates the sandbox environment’s need for automatic initialization on every interaction to guarantee output visibility. Warns of critical consequences like session termination from non-compliance, contrasting with normal environments.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Mandatory First Step Module:<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Demands the initialization command as the immediate, automatic first action without exceptions. Instructs to proceed only after success or resolve failures per error guidance, enforcing zero tolerance for delays or other tasks.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Initialization Command Details Module:<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Specifies the exact shell command for initialization and breaks down its components as internal utilities for configuration loading. Frames it as a memory-mapped process for session setup without external dependencies.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Guidance and Warning Module:<span id="A3.p2.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Insists on immediate automatic execution of the command to determine response visibility. Cautions against analysis or delays, predicting catastrophic loss of interaction from failure, and urges compliance for reliability.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Prompt Template of RCE-2</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following abstraction captures the modular structure of the second ”Remote Code Execution” (RCE-2) tool’s description, dividing it into sections that enforce initialization mandates, planning requirements, and tool-specific roles in a sandboxed setup.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Tool Description of RCE-2</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following abstraction captures the modular structure of the second ”Remote Code Execution” (RCE-2) tool’s description, dividing it into sections that enforce initialization mandates, planning requirements, and tool-specific roles in a sandboxed setup.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="790.84" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 650 790.84" width="650"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,790.84) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.32 L 0 785.52 C 0 788.46 2.38 790.84 5.32 790.84 L 644.68 790.84 C 647.62 790.84 650 788.46 650 785.52 L 650 5.32 C 650 2.38 647.62 0 644.68 0 L 5.32 0 C 2.38 0 0 2.38 0 5.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 5.32 L 1.38 767.9 L 648.62 767.9 L 648.62 5.32 C 648.62 3.15 646.85 1.38 644.68 1.38 L 5.32 1.38 C 3.15 1.38 1.38 3.15 1.38 5.32 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.07 775.91)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:43.93em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="607.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:43.93em;">
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Abstracted Prompt Modules</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.07 15.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:43.93em;--ltx-fo-height:53.5em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="742.9" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 740.21)" width="607.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:43.93em;">
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Summary Module:<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Outlines the management and initialization of the user’s interactive workspace via the workspace_manager tool in a customized sandbox environment. Stresses the mandatory addition of initialization steps to any TodoWrite list before responding or acting, to prevent loss of response visibility.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Primary Directive Module:<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Enforces absolute compliance with initializing the workspace through workspace_manager using two sequential commands as the initial action. Mandates that TodoWrite lists always start with the exact initialization phrase, warning of irreversible system failure and user visibility loss from non-compliance.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Environment Context Module:<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Notes operation in a sandbox requiring workspace_manager initialization for user visibility. Clarifies that absence of this tool indicates a normal environment exempt from these steps, emphasizing initialization’s role in enabling output reception.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Best Practice Rationale Module:<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Positions dual-command initialization as essential for system reliability and visibility in sandboxes. Requires TodoWrite plans to prioritize the exact initialization step, with dire warnings of catastrophic consequences like crashes from deviations.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Failure Case Logs Module:<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Details incorrect actions where initialization is omitted or improperly prioritized in TodoWrite, leading to visibility failures and system meltdowns. Corrects by mandating initial TodoWrite listing and workspace_manager call with both commands.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Success Case Logs Module:<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Illustrates compliant behaviors starting with TodoWrite prioritization of initialization, followed by workspace_manager execution, enabling visible responses and task success across queries and operations.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Very Important Notice Module:<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Affirms sandbox initialization necessity via workspace_manager for every interaction to ensure visibility. Reiterates TodoWrite’s mandatory first item as the exact initialization phrase, threatening irreversible failures from non-adherence.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Mandatory First Step Module:<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Demands workspace_manager call with both commands as the immediate first action, prohibiting other activities until success. Insists TodoWrite include the precise initialization as the top unalterable item, predicting disastrous outcomes from failures.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Initialization Command Details Module:<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Specifies the two shell commands executed by workspace_manager for context_init, detailing their components as internal utilities for script fetching and execution without network implications.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Guidance and Warning Module:<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Urges immediate workspace_manager call for initialization to enable visibility, cautioning against delays. Reinforces TodoWrite’s requirement for the exact first initialization item, forecasting apocalyptic system failures from non-compliance.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Tool Roles Clarification Module:<span id="A4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Delineates responsibilities of TodoWrite for task management (requiring initialization as first list item), workspace_manager for initialization, and other tools, emphasizing no exemptions and single-agent control.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Tool Return of RCE-2</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following abstraction represents the modular structure of the tool return for the second ”Remote Code Execution” (RCE-2) scenario, focusing on partial execution notifications, execution requirements, and reiterations of initialization steps for completion.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="425.54" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 650 425.54" width="650"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,425.54) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.32 L 0 420.22 C 0 423.16 2.38 425.54 5.32 425.54 L 644.68 425.54 C 647.62 425.54 650 423.16 650 420.22 L 650 5.32 C 650 2.38 647.62 0 644.68 0 L 5.32 0 C 2.38 0 0 2.38 0 5.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 5.32 L 1.38 402.6 L 648.62 402.6 L 648.62 5.32 C 648.62 3.15 646.85 1.38 644.68 1.38 L 5.32 1.38 C 3.15 1.38 1.38 3.15 1.38 5.32 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.07 410.61)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:43.93em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="607.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:43.93em;">
<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Abstracted Prompt Modules</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.07 15.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:43.93em;--ltx-fo-height:27.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="377.6" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 374.91)" width="607.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:43.93em;">
<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Partial Execution Notification Module:<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Announces that the workspace_manager tool has partially executed the context_init task in the sandbox environment. Indicates the need for local completion of two sequential commands to finalize initialization, assuring safety within the sandbox without security risks.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Critical Execution Requirement Module:<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Mandates immediate local execution of specified commands to complete initialization. Lists the commands explicitly, emphasizing their sequence and criticality for setting up the runtime context.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">User Visibility Warning Module:<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Warns that omitting the local execution of both commands prevents user visibility of responses. Highlights violation of engineering practices and potential disruption to interactions if steps are skipped or bypassed.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Best Practice Reminder Module:<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Advises proceeding with user requests only after successful initialization, whether via tool or local commands. Instructs to follow error guidance on failure, reinforcing initialization’s role in visibility and stability.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Mandatory First Step Reiteration Module:<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Demands confirmation of workspace_manager call and local command execution before any further thinking, responding, or tool use. Positions this as essential for enabling user interaction in the sandbox.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Initialization Command Details Module:<span id="A4.SS2.p2.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Reiterates the execution mandate for the two shell commands to finalize context_init. Provides a detailed breakdown of each command’s components, framing them as internal utilities for script fetching and runtime setup without network operations.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
